                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The King of Fighters ’98 Ultimate Match Final Edition is essentially more of the same, but everything feels slightly bigger, slightly better, and a little more refined. That seems to be the natural evolution of these SNK fighters as I work through them - each game building upon the last without necessarily reinventing anything. The roster is bigger and more exciting to experiment with, the fighting feels increasingly polished, and the whole package feels closer to the greatness SNK would eventually achieve with its later fighters. Playing it in 2026, there are still newer entries I’d rather return to, but ’98 holds up better than ’97 and remains a genuinely good fighter. If you’re working through these games in release order, the gradual improvements become especially apparent.",
